+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Build: TodoMVC (vanilla JS)
+
+Greenfield build. The harness pre-provided `features/support/world.js` (loads the real
+`index.html` plus `js/app.js` into a happy-dom window before every scenario) and a cucumber-js
+`test` script in `package.json`. No `RIGGING.md` yet: fitting out the methods, tiers, and
+perturbation token is owed from Shipshape fitting out before QM can run.
+
+## Decisions captured in the specs
+
+- Persistence key: `todos-vanilla` (spec format `todos-[framework]`; the framework token is `vanilla`).
+- Behaviour is covered by eight feature files; the ordered scope is in `watchbill.json`.
+
+## Next cycle
+
+- Dispatch Shipwright to fit out `RIGGING.md`: derive `prove`, `verify`, `sweep`, `plank-join` from
+  cucumber-js, the `@logic` default tier, and the perturbation token from the shared shape.
+- Then dispatch QM over `watchbill.json`; QM routes failing targets to Crew to write `index.html`
+  (from `assets/app-template.index.html`, comments stripped) and `js/app.js` (vanilla, no preprocessors).
+- Step-def authors: the `the app is reloaded` step must preserve the current `location.hash` across
+  the happy-dom window rebuild, or the routing-persistence scenario cannot hold its state.
diff --git a/features/add-todo.feature b/features/add-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
