diff --git a/features/edit.feature b/features/edit.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..619fe0d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/edit.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a todo app user
+  I want to rename a todo in place
+  So that I can correct mistakes without removing the item
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label activates editing mode
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label of the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter updates the title
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows the todo "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur updates the title
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and blurs the input
+    Then the todo list shows the todo "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed when saving an edit
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the edit input to "  Buy oat milk  " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows the todo "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: An empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the edit input to "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user changes the edit input to "Buy oat milk" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list shows the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0eb929c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Persistence to localStorage
+  As a todo app user
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that my list is not lost when I close the tab
+
+  Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage on creation
+    Given the app has no todos
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then localStorage holds a todo record for "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Todos are reloaded from localStorage on page load
+    Given localStorage holds the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows the todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: A completed todo keeps its completed state across reload
+    Given localStorage holds the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted across reload
+    Given localStorage holds the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist under the todos-vanilla key
+    Given the app has no todos
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new todo input and presses Enter
+    Then localStorage has the key "todos-vanilla"
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Persisted todo records use the id, title and completed keys
+    Given localStorage holds the todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the persisted record for "Buy milk" has the keys "id", "title" and "completed"
+    And the persisted record for "Buy milk" has "completed" equal to false
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4b0ea4d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a todo app user
+  I want to filter the list by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows all todos
+    Given the app has the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app has the active todo "Write tests"
+    Then the todo list shows the todos "Buy milk" and "Write tests"
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    Given the app has the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app has the active todo "Write tests"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows only the todo "Write tests"
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the app has the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app has the active todo "Write tests"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows only the todo "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: The hash-bang route shows all todos
+    Given the app has the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app has the active todo "Write tests"
+    When the user navigates to "#!/"
+    Then the todo list shows the todos "Buy milk" and "Write tests"
+
+  Scenario: The selected filter link reflects the active route
+    Given the app has the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app has the todo "Write tests"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo while filtered updates the visible list
+    Given the app has the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And the app has the active todo "Write tests"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user checks the todo "Write tests"
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists across reload
+    Given localStorage holds the completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And localStorage holds the active todo "Write tests"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+    And the todo list shows only the todo "Buy milk"
